From 1e40faadc04282fa17694def89b6e0f1c51847d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:36:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): archive then remove aged terminal scratch
 holding git clones [daveey]

Completion cleanup and gc_task_scratch keep every scratch tree with Git
metadata, so a worker's clone outlived its card forever (David-MBP: 2.7 GiB
of 10-23..10-26 leftovers pinning 9 install envs, ~0.2 GiB/day more).

gc_task_scratch now archives each standalone repo of a terminal scratch
workspace whose card finished more than kanban.worktree_retention_days ago
(default 7, 0 disables) to <kanban home>/archive/scratch/<board>/<task>/<rel>/
(commits.bundle of refs not reachable from remote-tracking refs, verified;
tracked.diff = git diff --binary HEAD; untracked.tar; meta.json), then removes
the tree and appends a workspace_archived event. A linked worktree or
submodule (.git file), a bare repo, scan errors, any failed archive step, a
live card, an active child or a live sharer keep it. Archiving runs outside
the board write lock; the owner is re-checked under the lock before the tree
is renamed away.
